  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 225 PM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nFriday night through Saturday night, an upper level trough will push \nfrom the Great Basin east through the Central to Southern Plains and \nalso send a cold front down through our region. Convergence along a \ntightening dry line could result in a few showers Saturday morning \nand afternoon, mainly north of I-10. Although there will be enhanced \nsoutherly winds in advance of the dry line and cold front, in \naddition to further warming of the 850 mb thermal ridge, cloud cover \nwill likely negate the warming potential, so highs right now are \nforecast to be in the low to mid 70s. The cold front will move \nthrough West Central Texas late Saturday evening through Sunday \nmorning, with cold air advection and surface high pressure behind \nthe front for Sunday and Monday, resulting in a cool-down for the \nstart of the week (highs Sunday in the mid 50s to low 60s, and highs \nMonday in the low to upper 50s, with lows Sunday morning in the mid \nto upper 40s, lows Monday morning in the mid 30s to low 40s, and \nlows Tuesday morning in the upper 30s to low 40s). \n\nStill a fair bit of uncertainty with the forecast for Tuesday \nthrough Thanksgiving. On Tuesday, some ensemble and deterministic \nmembers (most notably the 12Z GFS) are showing a deeper trough \npushing right through West Central Texas and bringing rain, while\nmost of the other ensemble and deterministic guidance keeps the \ntrough farther north, leaving us high and dry. Another potential \nsystem of uncertain magnitude/depth could move through the region \non Thanksgiving. Some ensemble/deterministic (including 12Z GFS \nand 12Z GEFS) guidance has a cutoff low/upper low moving through \nor near West Central Texas Thursday and/or Friday, bringing colder\nair and widespread precipitation, while other guidance (including\n12Z ECMWF, and 12Z EC Ensemble Mean) has a weaker trough that \nmoves through North Texas/Oklahoma and leaves our region with much\nless precipitation potential and not as cool.",
